  "_commit": {
    "id": "036c2d9d7462258dcb129e64a45dbecb312c22ef",
    "author": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "committer": "Patrick Aboyoun <aboyoun.patrick@gene.com>",
    "message": "feat: accept in-memory sf objects in st_join/st_join_table (0.99.8)\n\nst_join.DuckDBTable/st_join_table only accepted lazy DuckDBTable/\nDuckDBDataFrame objects for x/y. Closes a real gap flagged by a user\ncomparing against duckspatial::ddbs_intersects(), which accepts sf\nobjects on either side.\n\nNew internal .as_duckdb_table() materializes an in-memory sf object (or\na data.frame with an sfc or raw-WKB-list geometry column -- the latter\nmatching the shape as.data.frame() on a DuckDBDataFrame's own geometry\ncolumn produces) by converting its geometry to WKT (the same idiom\n.geom_to_sql() already uses for a single geometry), copying it into a\ntemp DuckDB table via copy_to(), then casting back to native GEOMETRY\nwith ST_GeomFromText(). Temp-table naming reuses DuckDBArray's\nPID+counter convention to avoid the dbplyr::unique_table_name()\nglobal-RNG collision class fixed there in 0.99.9. Chosen over\nwriteGeoParquet()+tempfile since that would pull in nanoparquet as a\nhard dependency and add disk I/O for what's typically the small side of\na join.\n\nThree independent review passes (two rounds, four reviewer agents total)\ncaught and fixed real problems before this shipped:\n- The redirect errors added to .geom_to_sql() pointed at spatialMatch()/\n  spatialJoin(), which don't exist in this package (those are\n  BiocDuckDB-level MultiAssaySpatialExperiment methods) -- corrected to\n  layerSpatialMatch(), st_join(), and st_join_table().\n- .as_duckdb_table()'s raw-WKB branch crashed on any NULL entry (the\n  common case of a DuckDBDataFrame's own geometry column, which\n  represents missing geometries as NULL), since sf::st_as_sfc.WKB()\n  asserts every element is raw with no NULL tolerance. Fixed by\n  substituting an empty geometry per NULL entry, wrapped in the same\n  tryCatch-to-friendly-error pattern writeGeoParquet() already uses.\n- Hardened the generated ST_GeomFromText(\"<col>\") SQL against a geometry\n  column name containing a literal double quote.\n\nAlso removed .spatialMatch_sql(",
    "time": 1792519461
  },
